<article class="env-lemma" id="0BZM">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BZM">Lemma <span data-tag="0BZM">47.14.2</span>.</a> Let $R \to A$ and $R \to R'$ be ring maps and $A' = A \otimes _ R R'$. Assume </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$A$ is pseudo-coherent as an $R$-module, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$R'$ has finite tor dimension as an $R$-module (for example $R \to R'$ is flat), 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$A$ and $R'$ are tor independent over $R$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then (<a href="/tag/0E29" data-tag="0E29">47.14.0.1</a>) is an isomorphism for $K \in D^+(R)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/0E2A" data-tag="0E2A">47.14.1</a> and More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0ATK" data-tag="0ATK">15.100.3</a> part (4). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>